WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.697 --> 00:00:17.322
filled her pockets with the two furry bundles, one for herself and one for Clara.

2
00:00:17.743 --> 00:00:22.547
The priest said he would deliver the rest of the kittens to Clara the following day.

3
00:00:23.008 --> 00:00:25.270
The boy with the organ led Heidi home.

4
00:00:26.371 --> 00:00:32.363
When they arrived, Sebastian pulled Heidi inside and slammed the door without noticing the little boy.

5
00:00:32.383 --> 00:00:33.283
"Hurry, miss!

6
00:00:33.463 --> 00:00:35.445
They are waiting for you at the dining room table.

7
00:00:35.865 --> 00:00:38.686
Fraulein looks like a loaded cannon ready to explode!"

8
00:00:39.987 --> 00:00:45.270
When Heidi stepped into the dining room, Fraulein did not look up and Clara didn't speak.

9
00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:51.994
Once Heidi was seated, Fraulein said icily, "I will punish you after dinner, Heidi.

10
00:00:52.674 --> 00:00:55.856
It was rude and wicked for you to leave the house without permission."

11
00:00:57.108 --> 00:00:59.130
"Meow!" came the answer back.

12
00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:01.211
Fraulein trembled with anger.

13
00:01:01.231 --> 00:01:04.713
"How dare you answer me as if it were a joke?!"

14
00:01:05.314 --> 00:01:07.435
"I didn't began Heidi.

15
00:01:07.455 --> 00:01:09.296
"Meow, meow!"

16
00:01:10.077 --> 00:01:10.938
she was interrupted.

17
00:01:12.278 --> 00:01:14.380
Sebastian's face broke into a smile.

18
00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.203
He had figured out what was going on and had to cover his mouth to keep from bursting

19
00:01:19.243 --> 00:01:19.864
into laughter.

20
00:01:20.244 --> 00:01:21.805
Clara looked at Heidi in alarm.

21
00:01:21.825 --> 00:01:23.146
"It's the kittens!"

22
00:01:23.786 --> 00:01:25.888
said Heidi, and the kittens meowed again.

23
00:01:27.028 --> 00:01:29.089
"What?! Kittens!"

24
00:01:29.629 --> 00:01:30.550
shrieked Fraulein.

25
00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.111
"Sebastian! Find the horrible things and take them away!"

26
00:01:35.932 --> 00:01:38.373
She leapt from the table and ran into the study.

27
00:01:38.393 --> 00:01:42.314
"You must help us," said Clara to Sebastian.

28
00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.616
"The kittens need a home," said Heidi.

29
00:01:45.636 --> 00:01:49.257
"I will see to it," answered Sebastian willingly.

30
00:01:49.998 --> 00:01:54.800
He found a warm basket and put the two kittens in a safe place where Fraulein was not

31
00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:55.580
likely to go.

32
00:01:56.288 --> 00:02:01.352
The next morning, Sebastian had just shown the tutor into the study when he heard the doorbell.

33
00:02:01.612 --> 00:02:06.255
He opened the door, and there in front of him was a messy little boy carrying a hand

34
00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:09.838
organ. "I want to see Clara," said the boy.

35
00:02:09.858 --> 00:02:11.699
"She owes me four pennies."

36
00:02:12.279 --> 00:02:12.880
"What for?"

37
00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.001
asked Sebastian.

38
00:02:14.021 --> 00:02:16.783
"For walking Heidi to the church and then home."

39
00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:20.946
"Oh," thought Sebastian, "this is more of Miss Heidi's mischief."

40
00:02:21.326 --> 00:02:24.068
He brought the boy into the house and showed him the study.

41
00:02:25.228 --> 00:02:27.049
"Clara is inside," he said.

42
00:02:27.069 --> 00:02:29.849
"Be sure to play your organ the moment you enter.

43
00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.270
Clara loves music."

44
00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.411
Fraulein, of course, ran to the study as soon as she heard the organ.

45
00:02:36.271 --> 00:02:40.392
Inside, the messy little boy was playing noisily and with great energy.

46
00:02:41.032 --> 00:02:43.493
Clara was delighted and Heidi clapped her hands.

47
00:02:45.094 --> 00:02:45.774
"Stop it!

48
00:02:46.174 --> 00:02:47.294
Stop it at once!"

49
00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.355
screamed Fraulein Rottenmeier.

50
00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:51.515
"Take him out, Sebastian.

51
00:02:51.796 --> 00:02:53.176
Take him out right now!"

52
00:02:53.768 --> 00:02:55.629
Sebastian pulled the boy out of the room.

53
00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.812
At the front door, he kindly gave the boy his money.

54
00:02:58.832 --> 00:03:04.315
"Here are four pennies from Miss Clara and three more for the music," said Sebastian.

55
00:03:05.456 --> 00:03:08.558
Fraulein decided to stay and watch the rest of the lesson.

56
00:03:09.158 --> 00:03:12.160
Soon, Heidi and Clara had settled down to their work again.

57
00:03:12.641 --> 00:03:16.603
There was a knock on the study door, and Sebastian entered with a large basket.

58
00:03:16.623 --> 00:03:20.546
"This was just delivered for you, miss," he said to Clara.

59
00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:21.847
"For me?"

60
00:03:22.507 --> 00:03:23.068
said Clara.

61
00:03:24.768 --> 00:03:29.790
"I think the girls should finish their lesson before the basket is opened," said Fraulein.

62
00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:33.651
Sebastian placed the basket on the floor and shut the door.

63
00:03:34.351 --> 00:03:40.933
The lesson continued quietly, and then, all of a sudden, Fraulein sprang up and jumped onto her chair.

64
00:03:41.593 --> 00:03:44.114
There were kittens scampering all over the floor.

65
00:03:45.254 --> 00:03:46.334
Clara was thrilled.

66
00:03:46.354 --> 00:03:49.375
"Oh, the dear little things!

67
00:03:50.295 --> 00:03:50.975
Look, Heidi!

68
00:03:51.316 --> 00:03:52.416
How pretty they are!"

69
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.443
Fraulein was so overcome with horror that she couldn't speak.

70
00:03:57.304 --> 00:04:02.148
At last, she found her voice and shrieked so loudly that the whole neighborhood heard.

71
00:04:02.168 --> 00:04:06.112
"Sebastian, Sebastian!"
